canonicalImage -- canonical model of the normalization of a plane curve
***********************************************************************

  * Usage: 
        R' = canonicalImage R
        R' = canonicalImage I
  * Inputs:
      * R, a *note ring: (Macaulay2Doc)Ring,, the homogeneous coordinate ring
        of a plane curve
      * I, an *note ideal: (Macaulay2Doc)Ideal,, homogeneous ideal of a plane
        curve
  * *note Optional inputs: (Macaulay2Doc)using functions with optional inputs,:
      * Conductor => ..., default value null
  * Outputs:
      * R', a *note ring: (Macaulay2Doc)Ring,, the homogeneous coordinate ring
        of the canonical image of the normalization

Description
===========

The output is the homogeneous coordinate ring of the canonical image of the
normalization the given curve.

For example,  a plane sextic with 4 nodes is a curve of genus 10-4 = 6, so its
canonical image is a curve of degree 10 in P5



