Conductor -- Option to avoid computation
****************************************

  * Usage: 
        M = geometricGenus(C,Conductor => cond)
  * Inputs:
      * C, a *note ring: (Macaulay2Doc)Ring,, 
      * cond, an *note ideal: (Macaulay2Doc)Ideal,, the conductor of C 

Description
===========

Computing the conductor involves computing the normalization, which is
potentially expensive. If it is known in advance (as in the case of an ordinary
multiple point) the user can insert it to avoid the computation.



See also
========

  * *note geometricGenus: geometricGenus, -- Geometric genus of a (singular)
    plane curve

