fromCoordinates -- Compute the ideal of a point from its coordinates
********************************************************************

  * Usage: 
        I = fromCoordinates(L,C)
        I = fromCoordinates(x,y,z, C)
  * Inputs:
      * L, a *note list: (Macaulay2Doc)List,, of three integers or field
        elements OR a list of lists of that type
      * x, a *note ring element: (Macaulay2Doc)RingElement,, 
      * y, a *note ring element: (Macaulay2Doc)RingElement,, 
      * z, a *note ring element: (Macaulay2Doc)RingElement,, integer or field
        coordinates of a point on C (assumed to be a plane curve)
      * C, a *note ring: (Macaulay2Doc)Ring,, the ring in which the ideal of
        the point will be created
  * Outputs:
      * I, an *note ideal: (Macaulay2Doc)Ideal,, of C, defining the subscheme
        corresponding to the list L of points.

Description
===========

Convenient way to compute the ideal of a point on a plane curve, when the point
is given by a list of its coordinates. If the coordinates are given as
integers, they are interpreted as elements of the coefficient field The script
returns an error if the point is not on the curve.

+---------------------------------------------------------+
|i1 : S = ZZ/101[a,b,c]                                   |
|                                                         |
|o1 = S                                                   |
|                                                         |
|o1 : PolynomialRing                                      |
+---------------------------------------------------------+
|i2 : C = S/ideal"a3+b3-c3"                               |
|                                                         |
|o2 = C                                                   |
|                                                         |
|o2 : QuotientRing                                        |
+---------------------------------------------------------+
|i3 : P = {0,1,1}                                         |
|                                                         |
|o3 = {0, 1, 1}                                           |
|                                                         |
|o3 : List                                                |
+---------------------------------------------------------+
|i4 : Q = {1,1,0}                                         |
|                                                         |
|o4 = {1, 1, 0}                                           |
|                                                         |
|o4 : List                                                |
+---------------------------------------------------------+
|i5 : fromCoordinates(P,C)                                |
|                                                         |
|o5 = ideal (a, - b + c)                                  |
|                                                         |
|o5 : Ideal of C                                          |
+---------------------------------------------------------+
|i6 : fromCoordinates({P,P},C)                            |
|                                                         |
|             2                             2           2 |
|o6 = ideal (a , - a*b + a*c, - a*b + a*c, b  - 2b*c + c )|
|                                                         |
|o6 : Ideal of C                                          |
+---------------------------------------------------------+

